<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03VB">Example <span data-tag="03VB">8.4.1.3</span>.</a> Let $\operatorname{Cat}$ denote the ordinary category whose objects are small categories and whose morphisms are functors, and let $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}\subset \operatorname{Cat}$ be the simplex category. Proposition <a data-tag="002Z" href="/tag/002Z">1.3.3.1</a> asserts that the restricted Yoneda embedding </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Cat}\rightarrow \operatorname{Fun}( \operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}^{\operatorname{op}}, \operatorname{Set}) = \operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}\quad \quad \operatorname{\mathcal{C}}\mapsto \operatorname{N}_{\bullet }(\operatorname{\mathcal{C}}) \]
</div>
<p> is fully faithful, so that $\operatorname{{\bf \Delta }}$ is a dense subcategory of $\operatorname{Cat}$. </p>
